      "writtenOn": "2024-08-06T01:05:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for the feedback. A few additional questions:\n* Why do the requests coming from submit_bio() have to be customized?\n* Is it clear that only a subset of the SCSI commands pass through __scsi_execute()? Only a subset of so-called pass-through requests pass through __scsi_execute. So-called filesystem requests (requests originating from filesystems) do not pass through __scsi_execute(). Some SCSI core submits pass-through requests without calling __scsi_execute() and calls blk_execute_rq() or blk_execute_rq_nowait() directly.\n* Has there been any attempt to send this functionality upstream?",
      "parentUuid": "b748ad91_18653b7d",
      "revId": "0e2c5ddb9f5cbbd89d8c17d9d55e17cb8ba17c7b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
